'''Hurricane Sahan''' was a catastrophic [[Capuyaquiran Sea]] hurricane that struck in 1969. It was the deadliest hurricane of the 20th century in the Capuyaquiran Sea, and the deadliest weather event of the 20th century in [[Lacashe]], the [[Bolodun and Kuvari Islands]], and the [[United Capuyaquiran Republic]].

Sahan formed in the mid-[[Aethiopean Ocean]] and moved westward toward the Capuyaquiran Sea before turning abruptly northwest toward [[Lacashe]] and [[Asikyira]]. The unexpected turn from a westward to a northward track made the storm exceptionally deadly, because coastal populations had prepared for a different trajectory. The hurricane killed at least 18,293 people — the deadliest hurricane in the Capuyaquiran Sea of the 20th century — and injured more than 135,300 people across the region.

The majority of the fatalities occurred in [[Lacashe]], where 12,420 people died in the southern part of the country, many of them flooded to death in their own homes. A further 4,442 died in [[Asikyira]], 1,215 on [[Bolodun]] in the [[Bolodun and Kuvari Islands]], and the remaining 216 deaths occurred in the [[United Capuyaquiran Republic]].

